(1179, 1174, 'bank_game_bot', 'Dice Bot', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 1, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<p><strong><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../assets/img/wired.png\"></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>TRIGGERS:</strong><br><img src=\"../../../../uploads/dicevalue.png\" width=\"198\" height=\"213\" align=\"right\">x1 WIRED Trigger: Dice Rolled<br><br><strong>EFFECTS:</strong>&nbsp;<br>x1 WIRED Effect: Bot Talks or Shouts to all Users<br><br><strong>CONDITIONS:<br></strong>x1 WIRED Condition: Triggering User is ON Furni<br><br><strong>OTHER:</strong><br>x1 Bot<br>x1 Dice<br><br><strong>STEP 1:</strong><br>Place down your <strong>WIRED Trigger: Dice Rolled</strong>- and stack the <strong>WIRED Effect: Bot Talks or Shouts to all Users</strong>, and <strong>WIRED Condition: Triggering User is ON Furni</strong> on top of it.<br><br><strong>STEP 2:</strong><br>Double click your <strong>WIRED Effect: Bot Talks or Shouts to all Users</strong>- enter the name you have given your bot, and in <strong>Message</strong> you can input something like: <em>%username%</em> has rolled a <em>%dicevalue%</em>!<br><br>This can be worded however you like, however <em>%dicevalue%</em> must be there for the bot to say the number rolled.<br><br><strong>STEP 3:<br></strong>Double click your&nbsp;<strong>WIRED Condition: Triggering User is ON Furni</strong> and select your host seat. This ensures the bot will only say the number when the host has rolled.<br><br><br>Congratulations! You\'ve just wired the most simple Dice Bot known to man! Be sure to test out your Wired by sitting in your hosts chair and rolling the dice! If set up properly, the bot will display the roll result once the dice has finished rolling.</p>', NULL, 0, ''),
(1180, 1174, 'auto_melting_Carpets', 'Melting Carpets', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 4, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<div class=\"desc\"><strong><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/assets/img/wired.png\"></strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"desc\"><strong>TRIGGERS:</strong><br>6x <em>User Says Exact Keyword</em><br>1x <em>User Walks On Furni</em><br>1x <em>User Walks Off Furni</em> <br><br><strong>EFFECTS:</strong><br>12x <em>Match Furni to State/Position/Height</em><br>1x <em>Teleport To Furni</em> <br><br><strong>CONDITIONS:</strong><br>6x <em>Group Member</em> <br><br><strong>Before you begin:</strong><br><em>Set up your game with 6 mats in the game area, and 6 mats in your wired area. I like to use black executive carpets and vanilla executive carpets.</em> <br><br><strong>STEP 1:</strong><br>Stack your wired as shown <em>(bottom: 2x <strong>EFFECT MATCH FURNI</strong>, middle: 1x <strong>TRIGGER USER SAYS EXACT KEYWORD</strong>, top: 1x CONDITION GROUP MEMBER)</em> <br><br><strong>STEP 2:</strong><br>Take the opposite <em><strong>EFFECT MATCH FURNI TO STATE/POSITION/HEIGHT</strong></em> and set it to <em><strong>TRIGGER USER SAYS EXACT WORD, CONDITION GROUP MEMBER</strong></em> and one mat in the game area, as well as one mat in the wired area. <br><br><strong>STEP 3:</strong><br>Next, you&rsquo;re going to switch the positions of the mats you just used. For this you will bring the mat from the game area down to the position of the mat in the wired area, and the one in the wired area to the position in the game area <br><br><strong>STEP 4:</strong><br>Move your <strong><em>TRIGGER USER SAYS EXACT KEYWORD</em> </strong>and<strong> <em>CONDITION GROUP MEMBER</em></strong> to the opposite side of the wired they were on. Then, take the opposite <em><strong>EFFECT MATCH FURNI TO STATE/POSITION/HEIGHT</strong></em> and set it to the two wired as well as the two mats just like you did in step 2. <br><em>*you are going to repeat this step 6 times for each mat, a new wired stack per mat.</em> <br><br><strong>STEP 5:</strong><br>Once you have 6 stacks that look like the picture above, take your <em><strong>TRIGGER USER SAYS EXACT KEYWORD</strong></em> and set your trigger word for each mat. Personally I use m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6. <br><br><strong>STEP 6:</strong><br>Lastly, make a stack of <strong><em>TRIGGER USER WALKS ON FURNI, TRIGGER USER WALKS OFF FURNI</em> </strong>and<strong> <em>EFFECT TELEPORT TO FURNI</em></strong>. Set your <em><strong>TRIGGER USER WALKS ON FURNI</strong></em> and <em><strong>TRIGGER USER WALKS OFF FURNI</strong></em> to the mats located in your wired area,, and set your <em><strong>EFFECT TELEPORT TO FURNI</strong></em> to a space in your waiting area. <br><br></div><center><img src=\"/assets/img/meltingcarpets.png\"></center>', NULL, 0, ''),
(1181, 1174, 'auto_colour_game', 'Colour Game', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 5, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<div class=\"desc\"><center><img src=\"../../../assets/img/wired.png\"></center><br><strong>TRIGGERS:</strong><br><img src=\"../../../assets/img/colourgame.png\" align=\"right\"> 5x <em>Repeat Effect</em><br>1x <em>User Stuff Collision</em><br>1x <em>Furni Double Clicked</em><br>1x <em>Group Member</em><br><br><br><strong>EFFECTS:</strong><br>4x <em>Don&rsquo;t Chase Top</em><br>1x <em>Teleport User</em><br>5x <em>Match Furni</em><br>1x <em>Random Effect</em> <br><br><strong>CONDITIONS:</strong><br>6x <em>Furni States and Positions Match</em><br>1x <em>Furni DOESN&rsquo;T Match</em><br>1x <em>Furni Matches</em><br><br><br><br><strong>STEP 1:</strong><br>Take 4 of your <em><strong>TRIGGER: REPEAT EFFECT</strong></em> and lay them out separately, set them to 0.5 delay. Then, stack <em><strong>EFFECT: DON&rsquo;T CHASE TOP</strong></em> on each of them, and <em><strong>CONDITION: FURNI STATES AND POSITIONS MATCH</strong></em> after on each stack. <br><br><strong>STEP 2:</strong><br>Set each of your <em><strong>EFFECT: DON&rsquo;T CHASE TOP</strong></em> to one of the rollers that users stand on after they&rsquo;ve picked their colour, one per stack. <br><br><strong>STEP 3:</strong><br>Take your <em><strong>CONDITION: FURNI STATES AND POSITIONS MATCH</strong></em> and set it to one of the coloured spheres you are using when it is out of its resting place. You will have one sphere selected per stack. Also, make sure current position in room is ticked. <br><br><strong>STEP 4:</strong><br>Make a new stack consisting of <em><strong>TRIGGER: USER STUFF COLLISION, EFFECT: TELEPORT USER</strong></em>, and <em><strong>CONDITION: FURNI MATCHES</strong></em>. Set your <em><strong>EFFECT: TELEPORT USER</strong></em> to an item in your waiting area, and set your CONDITION: FURNI TYPE MATCHES to all 4 of the rollers you are using. <br><br><strong>STEP 5:</strong><br>Make a new stack consisting of <em><strong>TRIGGER: FURNI DOUBLE CLICKED</strong></em>, 4x <em><strong>EFFECT: MATCH FURNI, CONDITION: GROUP MEMBER. EFFECT: RANDOM EFFECT</strong></em> and <em><strong>CONDITION: FURNI MATCHES.</strong></em> <br><br><strong>STEP 6:</strong><br>Take your <em><strong>TRIGGER: FURNI DOUBLE CLICKED</strong></em> and set it to the switch/button you will be using to send the spheres into the game area. Then, take 4x <em><strong>EFFECT: MATCH FURNI</strong></em>and set them to a sphere when they are in the game area in the position you want, one per wired box and make sure to tick current position in room. After that, take your <em><strong></strong><strong>CONDITION: FURNI STATES AND POSITIONS MATCH</strong></em> and set it to a random item in your game that will stay in that one place the entire game, make sure to click current position in room. <br><br><strong>STEP 7:</strong><br>Make another stack with the following wired: <em><strong>TRIGGER: REPEAT EFFECT, 1x EFFECT: MATCH FURNI, CONDITION: FURNI MATCHES</strong></em>, and <em><strong>FURNI DOESN&rsquo;T MATCH.</strong></em> <br><br><strong>STEP 8:</strong><br>First, set your <em><strong>TRIGGER: REPEAT EFFECT</strong></em>  to a 2 second delay. Then, take your <em><strong>EFFECT: MATCH FURNI STATE/HEIGHT/POSITION</strong></em> and set it to a 2 second delay, then set it to all 4 of your spheres when they are in their resting place, make sure to tick off current position in room. Do the exact same with your <em><strong>CONDITION: FURNI DOESN&rsquo;T MATCH</strong></em>. Lastly, take your <em><strong>CONDITION FURNI MATCHES </strong></em>and set it to a random item in your game, make sure to tick off current position in room. <br><br>Test this by having someone choose a colour in your game, flick the switch and if the ball matches the colour they&rsquo;re in it should kick them out.</div>', NULL, 0, ''),
(1182, 1174, 'fireball', 'Fireball ', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 2, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<div class=\"desc\"><center><img src=\"../../../assets/img/wired.png\"></center></div>\r\n<p><strong>TRIGGERS:</strong><br><img src=\"../../../../uploads/fbwired3.png\" align=\"right\">x1 WIRED Trigger: Furni State is Changed<br>x1 WIRED Trigger: User Walks ON Furni<br>x? WIRED Trigger: User Double Clicks Furni</p>\r\n<p><br><strong>EFFECTS:</strong><br>x? WIRED Effect: Move Furni to Furni<br>x1 WIRED Effect: Teleport User to Furni<br><br><strong>CONDITIONS:<br></strong>x? WIRED Condition: Triggering User ON Furni<br><br><strong>FURNITURE:<br></strong>x? Seat of Choice (for players)<br>x? Side Item (for opponents to click &amp; send)<br>x1 Floor Switch (or other Wired switch)<br>x1 Tile of Choice<br><br><strong>Before you begin:</strong><br>Set up your game with as many chairs as you&rsquo;d like (best range is from 12-16 chairs). Then, choose a Wired Switch to use as the trigger for sending the tile. Have the tile of your choice, and Wired Switch set up beside the host seat and you&rsquo;re set!<br><br><strong>STEP 1:</strong><br>Place down your <strong>WIRED Trigger: Furni State is Changed</strong>; open, and select the Wired Switch you have chosen as your trigger to move the Fireball tile.<br><br><strong>STEP 2:</strong><br>Place down your <strong>WIRED Effect: Move Furni to Furni</strong>; open, and press the&nbsp;<strong>Select Items&nbsp;</strong>button, underneath the title \"Furni to Move\" - select the tile you have chosen as the Fireball, and press finish.<br><br><strong>STEP 3:</strong><br>Underneath the title \"Furni to Move To\" press the <strong>Select Items</strong> button- select the seats you have chosen for your players to sit on, and press finish.<br><br><strong>STEP 4:</strong><br>Underneath the title \"Move Type\" - select how you\'d like the items to move. This is enitrely your preference. You may chose to send the item in a Random Order, order of your seat selection.</p>\r\n<p><strong>STEP 5:<br></strong>Underneath the title \"Rotate Furni\" - you may optionally select a rotation to apply to your selected tile once it has moved. You may skip this option if you do not wish to apply a rotation.<br><br><strong>STEP 6:&nbsp;<br></strong>Underneath the title \"Furni Placement\" - select the posistion you\'d like the item to appear from on your selected seats; infront, behind, to the left, to the right, or right on top of it.<br><br><strong>STEP 7:&nbsp;<br></strong>Underneath the title \"Avatar Condition\" - select the condition in which you\'d like your Fireball tile to move; to any selected furni, to selected furni with users, or to selected furni without users. This is entirely your choice in how you\'d like your game of Fireball to work. The fireball tile will move to the seat in accordance to whatever you set in this condition.<br><br><strong>Save your wired!<br><br></strong><strong>STEP 8:<br></strong>Place down <strong>WIRED Trigger: User Walks ON Furni</strong> - select your Fireball Tile as the item the user walks on.<br><br><strong>STEP 9:</strong><br>Place your <strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User to Furni</strong>- select the Fireball Tile, and a furniture you\'d like the user to teleport to if they lose.<br><br><strong>STEP 10:</strong><br>Set up (x) number of stacks (depending on how many player seats you\'ve set up), each stack containing one of each:<br><strong>WIRED Trigger: </strong>User Double Clicks<strong><br>WIRED Effect:</strong> Move Furni to Furni<br><strong>WIRED Condition:&nbsp;</strong>Triggering User ON Furni<br><br>- On each Trigger, select the chosen item beside the seat you want to send the tile to;<br>- On each Effect, select the players seat that is beside the item selected above- furni to move is your Fireball tile, furni to move to is the users seat, and chose your Furni Placement- ignore all other options on this Wired as they aren\'t needed for this part;<br>- On each Condition, select the chosen Fireball Tile.<br><br>Congratulations! You have successfully just set up Fireball using a total of 4 Wired Boxes! Be sure to test its functionality by flicking your selected switch to determine whether you\'ve achieved the desired results!</p>', NULL, 0, ''),
(1183, 1174, 'autogame_autoexit', 'Auto-Exit', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 3, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../assets/img/wired.png\"></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"float: right;\" src=\"../../../../uploads/tutorial02.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"146\" height=\"130\"><strong>TRIGGERS:<br></strong>x1 WIRED Trigger: Game Ends<br>x1 WIRED Trigger: User Walks ON Furni</p>\r\n<p><br><strong>EFFECTS:</strong><br>x1 WIRED Effect: Execute Stacks for Users<br>x2 WIRED Effect: Teleport User<br>x1 WIRED Effect: Toggle State<br><br><strong>FURNITURE:</strong>&nbsp;<br>x1 Gate (used as the entrance to your game)<br>x1 Counter (set to your preference for game length)<br><br><strong>STEP 1:<br></strong>Place down your wired as indicated to the right hand side of this guide: <br><br>- <strong>WIRED Trigger: User Walks on Furni, WIRED Effect: Toggle State</strong> being one stack;<br><br>&nbsp;- <strong>WIRED Trigger: Game Ends, WIRED Effect: Execute Stacks for Users</strong> being another stack;<br><br>- <strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User </strong>being on a tile by itself. <br><br> Place down your gate somewhere you\'d like the users to line-up and join in at.<br><br><strong>STEP 2:<br></strong>Set your<strong>&nbsp;WIRED Trigger: User Walks ON Furni</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>to the gate (or tile) you\'re using for the entrance of your game.&nbsp; Now, click on your&nbsp;<strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User </strong>box, and set it to teleport the user where you\'d like them to start inside of the game area.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>PRO TIP:</strong> Use \'Any Furni Without Users\' option on the&nbsp;<strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User</strong><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em>to prevent multiple users from being able to enter the game at the same time if doing a single player game.<em><br><br><strong>STEP 3:<br></strong></em>Set your&nbsp;<strong>WIRED Effect: Execute Stacks for Users</strong> to your preferred parameters-<br><br>- \"Select Furni\" is used as a detection area. Users on or near this area will be affected by the execution... Generally, selecting the items you used as your flooring is the best option to achieve desired results.<br><br>- \"Select Stack\" is used to select the stack of Wired Effects you want to execute... his can be used with any effect- in our case, we are going to use it <strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User</strong>- be sure to select this wired!<br><br>- \"Detection Mode\" is a condition mode, the option you select will indicate which users are affected by Wired Effects when executed- users actually on the selected furni, or simply near it.<br><br>- \"Bypass Conditions\" when selected will bypass any conditions on the selected stack.<br><br><strong>STEP 4:</strong><br>Set your&nbsp;<strong>WIRED Effect: Teleport User,&nbsp;</strong>the one we\'ve placed on a tile of its own, to a place you\'d like users to teleport to when they are automatically booted from the game.<br><br>Congratulations! You\'ve set up an auto-booter that can easily be applied to any auto-game you make! Be sure to test out your Wired by starting your counter, and standing in your detection area. When the counter runs down, you should automatically be teleported out of the game area to your selected furni.</p>', NULL, 0, ''),
(1184, 1174, 'auto_floor_is_lava', 'The Floor is Lava', 'pets3', 1, 80, 1, 6, '1', '1', '0', '0', '', '', '', '', NULL, '<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../assets/img/wired.png\"></p>\r\n<p><strong>Triggers:<br></strong>- x2 User Walk on Furni;<br>- x1 User Stuff Collision;<br>- x2 Repeat Effect;<br>- x1 Game Starts;<br>- x1 Game Ends.<br><strong><br></strong><strong>Effects:<br></strong>- x26 Match Posistion &amp; State/Height;<br>- x2 Give Effect;<strong><br></strong>- x1 Join Team;<br>- x1 User Leaves Team;<br>- x1 All Users Leave Team;<br>- x1 Teleport Team (Red in this example);<br>- x1 Freeze User;<br>- x1 Unfreeze User;<br>- x1 Move Furni Toward User.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Addons:<br></strong>- x1 Random Effect.<br><br><strong>Conditions:&nbsp;<br></strong>- x1 Triggerer is NOT on Furni.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Additional Materials:<br></strong>- x1 Counter/Timer of your Choice;<br>- x96 (or size of game field) Invisible Blocks (Walk);<br>- x96 Lava Blocks (amount depending on size of game field);<br>- x96 Dungeon Bricks (amount depending on size of game field);<br>- Wireds used in the &nbsp;<em><strong><a href=\"../../../community/articles/wired-guide-auto-game-auto-exit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Autogame Auto-Exit</a></strong></em> tutorial setup.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<p><strong>STEP ONE</strong><br>To ensure the complete automation of <em><strong>The Floor is Lava</strong></em>, you must first follow and complete the tutorial for&nbsp;<em><strong><a href=\"../../../community/articles/wired-guide-auto-game-auto-exit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Autogame Auto-Exit</a>&nbsp;</strong></em>in the room you intend to use for your game. We will not go over these steps in this guide... Following and completing the tutorial above will ensure users are automatically booted from the game once the timer has run out- effectively making it automatic.&nbsp;<br><br><br><br><strong>STEP TWO<br></strong>Set up your play area. placing your lava blocks down first to cover the entire field, and placing the Dungeon Bricks over top of those.&nbsp; I\'ve set my <strong>Lava Blocks</strong> to have a bh of 0 and the <strong>Dungeon Bricks</strong> have a bh of 0.2, this way the bricks overlap the lava, making it seem like the floor gives out underneath the user, sending them into the lava.<br><br><br><br><strong>STEP THREE<br></strong>For your first stack, place down<strong> </strong><em>User Stuff Collision</em><em>, User Walks on Furni, Give User Effect, Freeze User, Teleport User and&nbsp; Triggerer is NOT on</em><em>&nbsp;Furni Conditions:</em><img style=\"float: right;\" src=\"../../../../storage/tinymce-images/RQClLPRF6UHVHubkL6pwHQT2UuSbuNwgHpNXhImE.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"127\" height=\"155\"><em><strong><br></strong></em>- <strong>User Stuff Collision:</strong> <em>Leave as is;<br></em>-&nbsp;<strong>Walks on Furni:&nbsp;</strong><em>Select all of your lava blocks;</em><br>-&nbsp;<strong>Give Effect:&nbsp;</strong><em>Set the effect id to 25;</em><br>-&nbsp;<strong>Freeze User:</strong> <em>You can leave this as is- it just ensures the player cant move after dying;</em><br>- <strong>Teleport User:&nbsp;</strong><em>Select the furniture you want users to teleport on to when they lose the game, adding a 2 second delay.<br>- </em><strong>Triggerer is NOT on Furni:&nbsp;</strong><em>Select all of your invisible blocks in the fame field, use :invisibleblock command to hide them afterwards.</em><em><br><br><br><br></em><strong>STEP FOUR<br></strong>For your second stack, place down <em>User Walk on Furni, Give User Effect, Unfreeze User and User Leaves Team:<strong><br></strong></em>- <strong>User Walks on Furni:&nbsp;</strong><em>Select the item you used as the \"losing game\" tile in Step 3;<br>-&nbsp;</em><strong>Give Effect:</strong> <em>Set the effect id to 0;<br>- </em><strong>Unfreeze User: </strong><em>You may leave this as is- alternatively you may insert a message into it to indicate the user has lost;<br>- </em><strong>User Leaves Team:</strong><em><strong> </strong>Leave this as it is.<br><br><br><br></em><strong>STEP FIVE<br></strong>Next, we\'re going to set up the wired that initiates the game once the Counter/Timer has started. Simply set the time to your desired length of game. This can be set to whatever you\'d like and should be scaled to the size of your game field. Once this has been done we can start setting up our next stacks of wired.</p>\r\n<p><strong><img style=\"float: right;\" src=\"../../../../storage/tinymce-images/kEB2K0mddr8EK541gWH1hWb3abPK5pgCYqQ4ZG0b.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"160\" height=\"452\"></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>5.1) </strong>For your third stack, place down the&nbsp;<em>Game Starts, Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height</em> Wireds in one stack, place down the<em> Repeat Effect</em> <em>Trigger</em> on a tile of its own<em>:</em><br>-&nbsp;<strong>Game Starts:</strong> <em>Leave this as is;</em><br>- <strong>Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height:&nbsp;</strong><em> Select the&nbsp;<strong>Wired Trigger: Repeat Effect&nbsp;</strong>and place it on top of the Random Effect and Match x24 Stack. Open the wired, and match the&nbsp;<strong>Repeat Effect</strong> to the current posistion in room.</em><br><br><strong>5.2)</strong> <strong>This stack should already exist if you completed the <em><a href=\"../../../community/articles/wired-guide-auto-game-auto-exit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Autogame Auto-Exit</a> Tutorial. In which case, simply ass the Match Posistion &amp; State Wireds- if you have not completed the tutorial, then do the entire thing.<br><br></em>&nbsp;</strong>For your fourth stack, place down the<em> <strong>G</strong>ame Ends, x2 Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height, Teleport Team (Red) and All Users<strong> </strong>Leave Team&nbsp;</em>wireds. Its important to ensure all Dungeon Bricks are in proper place for a fresh game:<br>-&nbsp;<strong>Game Ends:&nbsp;</strong><em>Leave this as is;<br></em>- <strong>Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height #1</strong>: <em>Ensure <strong>Wired Trigger: Repeat Effect&nbsp;</strong>is on an empty tile on its own, set to match posistion;&nbsp;<br>- <strong>Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height #2</strong>:&nbsp;Select all of your <strong>Dungeon Bricks&nbsp;</strong>to match posistion in room with a 1.5 second delay;<br></em>- <strong>Teleport Team (Red):</strong> <em>Select the tile you used as the \"losing tile\" in the above steps to teleport the users to, add a 5 second delay;</em><br>- <strong>All Users Leave Team:</strong> <em>Set a 5.5 second delay to this wired.</em><br><em>* you may alternative add a Match Posistion &amp; State and Height Wired to open your entrance gate once the game has ended.</em><br><br><strong>5.3)</strong> For your fifth stack,&nbsp;<em>&nbsp;</em>and then<em> Random Effect </em>and<em> x24 Match Posistion &amp; State<strong> &amp; </strong>Height&nbsp;</em>on a separate tile. (The amount of Match wired needed depends solely on your size of your game field. My game field is 96 tiles, meaning I need 24 of these wireds to move a 2x2 area of Dungeon Bricks.):<em><br>- <strong>Repeat Effect:</strong> Repeat Effect we previously wired in 5.2 to move onto this stack when the game ended- leave as is;<br></em><strong>- x24 Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height:</strong> <em>For each individual wired, select 4 of your <strong>Dungeon Bricks</strong>, moving them off-map to somewhere hidden. Open the Wired, and match the posistion in the room to where they are hidden. The posistion of these blocks should automatically reset after the clock ends if you followed the above step- it might be a good idea to set up a separate stack containing <strong>User</strong> <strong>Says Keyword Trigger and Match Posistion &amp; State &amp; Height for the Dungeon Bricks.<br>-&nbsp;Random Effect Addon: </strong>Leave this as is;<strong><br><br><br><br><br></strong></em><strong>STEP SIX<img style=\"float: left;\" src=\"../../../../storage/tinymce-images/kg8Kb9zUOO2LALoU5g9NFw7lHiYmzmODzVogZYXF.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"92\" height=\"93\"><br></strong>It\'s time to set up the trigger that boots you from the game! To achieve this,&nbsp; we need two stacks, one of which we have already set up in <em>Step Three.&nbsp; </em>We did this in advanced, as the invisible blocks must be above the Dungeon Bricks. For the next stack, we\'re going to need x1 <em>Repeat Effect Trigger, x1 Move Furni Toward User Effect</em> and <em>x96 Invisible Tiles (Walk):<br><strong><br>- </strong></em><strong>x96 Invisible Tiles (Walk):&nbsp;</strong><em>Place down over top of the Dungeon Bricks;</em><em><strong><br></strong>- </em><strong>Repeat Effect:</strong><em><strong> </strong>Leave as is;<br>- </em><strong>Move Furni Toward User:</strong><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Select all of the Invisible Tiles (Walk) you just placed down.<br><br></em><em>Simply use the :invisibleblock command to hide the invisible blocks.<br><br><br><br></em></p>\r\n<p><strong>STEP SEVEN<br></strong>It\'s important to now test your wiring thoroughly. If you have followed the above steps properly, the game should function without any issues. Begin testing by entering your game as a normal player would. Ensure you have set up the auto-exit using the tutorial mentioned at the start of this article for a smooth game. Whenever you are ready, simple start the clock to begin your game. As the tiles move away, any users falling into the lava below should be burned and automatically teleported out of the game. When the clock ends, your Dungeon Bricks should return to place, and any remaining users should tele out- effectively resetting the game for the next round.&nbsp;</p><br><img style=\"float: right;\" src=\"../../../../storage/tinymce-images/jGEES1wVbO3zeKyiyXbInO0Rmw3eXOziQlXVMNzz.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"320\" height=\"484\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, 0, ''),
